## `numpy.array`

The most important data structure for numerical computation is `numpy.array`.

::: {#f0fb24d5 .cell execution_count=24}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import numpy as np

x = np.array([1, 2, 3, 4])
x
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=24}
```
array([1, 2, 3, 4])
```
:::
:::


An array has a shape.

::: {#7d5f6e68 .cell execution_count=25}
``` {.python .cell-code}
x.shape
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=25}
```
(4,)
```
:::
:::


For this object, the shape is `(4,)`. This means it is a one-dimensional array with 4 elements.

### One-Dimensional Arrays

A one-dimensional array behaves like a vector.

::: {#99775a13 .cell execution_count=26}
``` {.python .cell-code}
x = np.array([10, 20, 30])
x.ndim
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=26}
```
1
```
:::
:::


::: {#65d41b7b .cell execution_count=27}
``` {.python .cell-code}
x.shape
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=27}
```
(3,)
```
:::
:::


Indexing is zero-based.

::: {#9bd57292 .cell execution_count=28}
``` {.python .cell-code}
x[0]
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=28}
```
np.int64(10)
```
:::
:::


Vectorized arithmetic works similarly to R.

::: {#af5c2b40 .cell execution_count=29}
``` {.python .cell-code}
x + 1
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=29}
```
array([11, 21, 31])
```
:::
:::


::: {#b7ff1ece .cell execution_count=30}
``` {.python .cell-code}
x * 2
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=30}
```
array([20, 40, 60])
```
:::
:::


::: {#5ee14ed3 .cell execution_count=31}
``` {.python .cell-code}
np.mean(x)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=31}
```
np.float64(20.0)
```
:::
:::


### Two-Dimensional Arrays

A two-dimensional array is like a matrix.

::: {#60179689 .cell execution_count=32}
``` {.python .cell-code}
X = np.array(
    [
        [1, 2],
        [3, 4],
        [5, 6],
    ]
)

X
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=32}
```
