## `matplotlib` Basics

These notes use only basic `matplotlib`.

The standard import is:

::: {#4769514e .cell execution_count=61}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
```
:::


### Scatter Plot

::: {#b2983b6e .cell execution_count=62}
``` {.python .cell-code}
x = np.array([1, 2, 3, 4])
y = np.array([1.1, 2.0, 2.8, 4.2])

plt.scatter(x, y)
plt.xlabel("x")
plt.ylabel("y")
plt.title("Scatter Plot")
plt.show()
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}
![](python_files/figure-html/cell-63-output-1.png){width=589 height=449}
:::
:::


### Line Plot

::: {#83bb99dc .cell execution_count=63}
